Figure 10 demonstrates the uptake of AF647-labeled Nano-11 (red) and its associated antigen (OVA) by inflammatory cells in the skeletal muscle 24 hours post-injection. The top row, representing Nano-11+OVA injection, shows intracellular Nano-11 within Mac-2+ monocytes/macrophages and MHCII+ cells (green), indicating efficient phagocytosis. In contrast, soluble OVA alone (bottom row) induced minimal inflammatory cell recruitment and antigen uptake. This highlights Nano-11's capacity to induce local inflammation and enhance antigen delivery to key antigen-presenting cells like monocytes and MHCII+ cells.